# Brewfile-formatted, but NOT run via `brew bundle`.
#
# These apps auto-update themselves, which fights Homebrew's own updates
# (brew thinks it's up to date, the app's self-updater disagrees, and
# `brew upgrade` / `brew bundle` can't cleanly manage the installed version).
#
# ~/.config/yadm/bootstrap iterates over the `brew`/`cask` lines below and,
# for each one not already installed, runs `brew install` once to get it
# onto the machine. After that, the app manages its own updates.

cask "bitwarden"
cask "discord"
cask "ticktick"
